# This CITATION.cff file was generated for Kavach v2.
# Validate with: pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its evaluation results, please cite it using the
  metadata below. Results are measured on the ULB credit-card dataset and validate
  pipeline mechanics only; they are not evidence of fraud detection on UPI/IMPS data.
type: software
title: "Kavach v2: a bank-agnostic, federated, threat-resilient fraud intelligence layer"
abstract: >-
  Research prototype of a fraud-intelligence layer for Indian retail banking: a
  bank-adapter registry with a fixed feature contract, federated per-bank threshold
  learning with coordinate-median (Byzantine-robust) aggregation, prompt-injection
  hardening for LLM-based classification, and an evaluation harness. Key measured
  findings on a five-bank partition of the ULB card-fraud dataset: federation's
  cold-start advantage is driven by positive-class scarcity rather than sample
  scarcity; one poisoned participant collapses FedAvg (0.682 to 0.001 AUC-PR) while
  coordinate-median holds (0.691); per-bank calibrated thresholds deliver
  alert-budget adherence but not additional detection.
authors:
  # TODO(owner): replace with your name, ORCID and affiliation before publishing.
  - name: "Kavach v2 contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dev-erebus/kavach-v2"
